<!doctype html>
{%- comment -%}
  The accent colour goes on the root element, not on <body>: the stylesheet
  derives three tints from it in a `:root` rule, and a custom property is
  resolved on the element it is declared for.
{%- endcomment -%}
<html lang="{{ page.locale }}" style="--accent: {{ theme.options.accent }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  {%- comment -%}
    The home page describes itself in the site owner's words. The tagline and
    the description Mallok derives from it are the page's language's. The
    option is for a site that wants more than a tagline under its name in a
    search result.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% assign summary = page.description %}
  {% if page.kind == "home" and theme.options.home_description != blank %}{% assign summary = theme.options.home_description %}{% endif %}
  {%- comment -%}
    The pages of one list would otherwise all carry one title.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    A block, so that a layout whose page Mallok has no title for — a plugin's
    page, which is titled with the site's name unless the plugin has words —
    can say what it is in this theme's own.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <title>{% block title %}{% if page.kind == "home" %}{{ site.name }}{% if site.tagline != "" %} — {{ site.tagline }}{% endif %}{% else %}{{ page.title }}{% if page.kind == "list" and list.page > 1 %}, {{ t.page }} {{ list.page }}{% endif %} — {{ site.name }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}</title>
  {% if summary != "" %}<meta name="description" content="{{ summary }}">{% endif %}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ page.canonical }}">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ site.name }}">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{% if page.kind == "home" %}{{ site.name }}{% else %}{{ page.title }}{% endif %}">
  {% if summary != "" %}<meta property="og:description" content="{{ summary }}">{% endif %}
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ page.canonical }}">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  {%- comment -%}
    page.head carries hreflang (with x-default) and the structured data, both
    emitted by Mallok. Leaving it out breaks the site's multilingual indexing,
    which is the one thing a theme must never be able to do by accident.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {{ page.head }}
  {%- comment -%}
    The two fonts every page draws its first screen with. Without the hint the
    browser finds them only after it has parsed the stylesheet.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ theme.asset_base }}/fonts/inter-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ theme.asset_base }}/fonts/space-grotesk-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ theme.asset_base }}/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">{{ t.skip }}</a>
  {% render "partials/header" %}
  <main id="main">{% block content %}{% endblock %}</main>
  {% render "partials/footer" %}
</body>
</html>
